73. Important Implementation Rule
The new website must be developed as a content-driven platform, not as a collection of hard-coded pages. Administrators must be able to change the following without any source-code changes:
•Student statistics
•Services
•Program details
•Team members
•Projects
•Testimonials
•Blog posts
•Events
•Contact information
•Certifications
•SEO metadata
74. Final Product Vision
The renewed NK SkillEdge website should function as more than a company brochure — it should become a central digital platform for the organization, supporting:
Branding + Student Acquisition + Training Registration + Internship Management + Client Acquisition + Project Portfolio + Content Marketing + Career Opportunities + Lead Management
NK SkillEdge is not only a training organization; it is a technology, skill-development, and digital-solutions ecosystem focused on shaping skills and building futures.
The new website must be modern enough for current users while maintaining an architecture capable of supporting future products such as an LMS, student portals, CRM, online payments, certificate verification, and AI-powered services.